# Security policy

## Supported versions

Only the latest release on `main` gets security fixes.

## Reporting a vulnerability

Please do not open a public issue for security problems. Report them privately through GitHub:
open the [Security tab](https://github.com/@project_REPOSITORY@/security) and choose
**Report a vulnerability**
([direct link](https://github.com/@project_REPOSITORY@/security/advisories/new)).

Include what is affected, how to reproduce it, and what an attacker could do with it. You should get
an answer within a week. Once a fix is released, the advisory is published and you are credited
unless you prefer not to be.

Problems in third-party libraries that @project_NAME@ uses belong with their maintainers. If
@project_NAME@ pins a vulnerable version, do report that here.
